PART 2 — INSTALL OLLAMA
Download the Windows version from:
Ollama Windows download
Install it normally.
Open a new PowerShell:
ollama --version
You should see an Ollama version.
Test it:
ollama
If Ollama starts, press Ctrl+C.
________________________________________
PART 3 — DOWNLOAD YOUR FIRST AI MODEL
For Day 1, use Qwen3 4B:
ollama pull qwen3:4b
Check that it exists:
ollama list
You should see something similar to:
NAME
qwen3:4b
Start it:
ollama run qwen3:4b
Test:
Explain what systemctl does in Linux.
Then:
/bye
If your computer has limited RAM
Use:
ollama pull qwen3:1.7b
and later change the Python configuration from:
qwen3:4b
to:
qwen3:1.7b
PART 4 — TEST THE AI API
Ollama provides a local API that our Python program will use.
Open another PowerShell window.
Run:
Invoke-RestMethod `
  -Uri "http://localhost:11434/api/chat" `
  -Method POST `
  -ContentType "application/json" `
  -Body '{"model":"qwen3:4b","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Explain SSH to a beginner system administrator."}],"stream":false}'
If you get an AI response, this part is working.
Your architecture is now:
Python/Applications
       │
       ▼
localhost:11434
       │
       ▼
    Ollama
       │
       ▼
    Qwen3
